______ the book already.","options":["had read","has read","reads","is reading"],"answer":"had read","explanation":"Reported speech: past perfect for completed action.","points":1},{"id":5521,"question":"Please ______ the lights before leaving.","options":["turn off","turn on","turn up","turn down"],"answer":"turn off","explanation":"''Turn off'' means to stop the power supply.","points":1},{"id":5522,"question":"She ______ her old clothes.","options":["threw away","threw up","threw in","threw out"],"answer":"threw away","explanation":"''Threw away'' means to discard something.","points":1},{"id":5523,"question":"He ______ his jacket because it was cold.","options":["put on","put off","put up","put down"],"answer":"put on","explanation":"''Put on'' means to wear clothing.","points":1},{"id":5524,"question":"I need to ______ this report by Friday.","options":["finish off","finish up","finish off","finish on"],"answer":"finish off","explanation":"''Finish off'' means to complete something.","points":1},{"id":5525,"question":"She ______ her old car for a new one.","options":["traded in","traded up","traded off","traded on"],"answer":"traded in","explanation":"''Traded in'' means to exchange something for credit.","points":1},{"id":5526,"question":"He ______ his friends after a long time.","options":["ran into","ran over","ran through","ran away"],"answer":"ran into","explanation":"''Ran into'' means to meet someone unexpectedly.","points":1},{"id":5527,"question":"We need to ______ this meeting.","options":["set up","set off","set back","set down"],"answer":"set up","explanation":"''Set up'' means to arrange or organize.","points":1},{"id":5528,"question":"She ______ her work until midnight.","options":["stayed up","stayed in","stayed on","stayed out"],"answer":"stayed up","explanation":"''Stayed up'' means to remain awake late.","points":1},{"id":5529,"question":"He ______ his homework before playing games.","options":["got through","got over","got along","got up"],"a