ons":["Don''t be sad about something that''s happened","Don''t drink milk","Don''t cry","Don''t spill things"],"answer":"Don''t be sad about something that''s happened","explanation":"''Cry over spilt milk'' means to be upset about something that can''t be changed.","points":1},{"id":5539,"question":"He ''burned the midnight oil'' studying.","options":["Studied late at night","Burned something","Was angry","Was tired"],"answer":"Studied late at night","explanation":"''Burn the midnight oil'' means to work late into the night.","points":1},{"id":5540,"question":"She ''bit off more than she could chew''.","options":["Took on too much","Ate too much","Was hungry","Was greedy"],"answer":"Took on too much","explanation":"''Bit off more than she could chew'' means to take on more than one can handle.","points":1},{"id":5541,"question":"He ''let the cat out of the bag''.","options":["Revealed a secret","Lost his cat","Was careless","Was afraid"],"answer":"Revealed a secret","explanation":"''Let the cat out of the bag'' means to reveal a secret.","points":1},{"id":5542,"question":"They ''hit it off'' at the party.","options":["Got along well immediately","Fought","Were bored","Left early"],"answer":"Got along well immediately","explanation":"''Hit it off'' means to get along well from the start.","points":1},{"id":5543,"question":"She ''under the weather'' today.","options":["Feeling sick","Outside","Wet","Cold"],"answer":"Feeling sick","explanation":"''Under the weather'' means feeling ill or unwell.","points":1},{"id":5544,"question":"He ''cost an arm and a leg''.","options":["Very expensive","Cheap","Free","Heavy"],"answer":"Very expensive","explanation":"''Cost an arm and a leg'' means very expensive.","points":1},{"id":5545,"question":"She ''a piece of cake''.","options":["Very easy","Delicious","Sweet","Cake"],"answer":"Very easy","explanation":"''A piece of cake'' means something very easy to do.","points":1},{"id":5546,"question":"He ''barking up the wrong tree''.","options":["Making a wrong assumption","Loving dogs","In a forest","Noisy"],"answer":"Making a wrong assumption","explanation":"''Barking up the wrong tree'' means pursuing a mistaken course of action.","points":1},{"id":5547,"question":"She ''the ball is in your court''.","options":["It''s your decision","Playing tennis","Sports","Exercise"],"answer":"It''s your decision","explanation":"''The ball is in your court'' means it''s someone''s turn to make a decision.","points":1},{"id":5548,"question":"He ''beat around the bush''.","options":["Avoids the main topic","Gardening","Running","Fighting"],"answer":"Avoids the main topic","explanation":"''Beat around the bush'' means to avoid talking about the main topic.","points":1},{"id":5549,"question":"She ''call it a day''.","options":["Stop working","Phone someone","Daytime","End call"],"answer":"Stop working","explanation":"''Call it a day'' means to stop working on something.","points":1},{"id":5550,"question":"He ''cut to the chase''.","options":["Get to the point","Run fast","Chase someone","Film scene"],"answer":"Get to the point","explanation":"''Cut to the chase'' means to get to the point without wasting time.","points":1},{"id":5551,"question":"What does ''Actions speak louder than words'' mean?","options":["Doing is more important than saying","Talk is cheap","Words hurt","Actions are loud"],"answer":"Doing is more important than saying","explanation":"This proverb means that what you do is more important than what you say.","points":1},{"id":5552,"question":"What does ''A penny saved is a penny earned'' mean?","options":["Saving money is like earning it","Pennies are valuable","Earn more money","Spend wisely"],"answer":"Saving money is like earning it","explanation":"This proverb means that saving money is as good as making money.","points":1},{"id":5553,"question":"What does ''Better late than never'' mean?","options":["It''s okay to be late","Doing something late is better than not doing it","Never be late","Always be early"],"answer":"Doing something late is better than not doing it","explanation":"This proverb means that doing something late is better than not doing it at all.","points":1},{"id":5554,"question":"What does ''Don''t count your chickens before they hatch'' mean?","options":["Don''t assume outcomes before they happen","Count carefully","Chickens are valuable","Wait for results"],"answer":"Don''t assume outcomes before they happen","explanation":"This proverb means not to make plans based on events that haven''t happened yet.","points":1},{"id":5555,"question":"What does ''Every cloud has a silver lining'' mean?","options":["There''s something good in every bad situation","Clouds are shiny","Weather is good","Silver is valuable"],"answer":"There''s something good in every bad situation","explanation":"This proverb means that every difficult situation has a positive aspect.","points":1},{"id":5556,"question":"What does ''The early bird catches the worm'' mean?","options":["Those who act first get the advantage","Birds eat worms","Wake up early","Catch things"],"answer":"Those who act first get the advantage","explanation":"This proverb means that people who act promptly have an advantage.","points":1},{"id":5557,"question":"What does ''Practice makes perfect'' mean?","options":["Regular practice improves skills","Perfection is impossible","Practice is easy","Mistakes are bad"],"answer":"Regular practice improves skills","explanation":"This proverb means that doing something repeatedly improves your ability.","points":1},{"id":5558,"question":"What does ''Don''t put all your eggs in one basket'' mean?","options":["Diversify your investments","Eggs break easily","Carry carefully","Don''t be greedy"],"answer":"Diversify your investments","explanation":"This proverb means not to risk everything on a single plan.","points":1},{"id":5559,"question":"What does ''When in Rome, do as the Romans do'' mean?","options":["Follow local customs when traveling","Visit Rome","Romans are good","Travel often"],"answer":"Follow local customs when traveling","explanation":"This proverb means to follow the customs of the place you''re visiting.","points":1},{"id":5560,"question":"What does ''You can''t judge a book by its cover'' mean?","options":["Appearances can be deceiving","Books are good","Covers are nice","Read books"],"answer":"Appearances can be deceiving","explanation":"This proverb means that outward appearance doesn''t tell the whole story.","points":1},{"id":5561,"question":"What does ''Rome wasn''t built in a day'' mean?","options":["Great things take time","Rome is old","Build slowly","Be patient"],"answer":"Great things take time","explanation":"This proverb means that important work takes time to complete.","points":1},{"id":5562,"question":"What does ''Where there''s a will, there''s a way'' mean?","options":["Determination leads to success","Will is strong","Ways are many","Find paths"],"answer":"Determination leads to success","explanation":"This proverb means that if you''re determined enough, you can find a method.","points":1},{"id":5563,"question":"What does ''Curiosity killed the cat'' mean?","options":["Being too curious can be dangerous","Cats are curious","Don''t ask questions","Cats die"],"answer":"Being too curious can be dangerous","explanation":"This proverb warns against unnecessary curiosity or risk-taking.","points":1},{"id":5564,"question":"What does ''Don''t cry over spilt milk'' mean?","options":["Don''t be upset about things that can''t be changed","Milk spills easily","Clean up","Be careful"],"answer":"Don''t be upset about things that can''t be changed","explanation":"This proverb means there''s no use being upset about past mistakes.","points":1},{"id":5565,"question":"What does ''Barking up the wrong tree'' mean?","options":["Making a false assumption","Dogs bark","Climb trees","Wrong direction"],"answer":"Making a false assumption","explanation":"This proverb means pursuing a mistaken course of action.","points":1},{"id":5566,"question":"What does ''A picture is worth a thousand words'' mean?","options":["Images convey meaning better than text","Pictures are expensive","Words are few","Take photos"],"answer":"Images convey meaning better than text","explanation":"This proverb means that a visual representation can tell a story better than words.","points":1},{"id":5568,"question":"What does ''Don''t bite the hand that feeds you'' mean?","options":["Don''t harm those who help you","Bite gently","Eat carefully","Be grateful"],"answer":"Don''t harm those who help you","explanation":"This proverb means don''t act ungratefully toward someone who supports you.","points":1},{"id":5569,"question":"What does ''Good things come to those who wait'' mean?","options":["Patience is rewarded","Wait always","Good things are rare","Be patient"],"answer":"Patience is rewarded","explanation":"This proverb means that if you''re patient, you''ll eventually get what you want.","points":1},{"id":5570,"question":"What does ''Necessity is the mother of invention'' mean?","options":["Difficulties inspire new solutions","Mothers invent","Necessities are good","Invent things"],"answer":"Difficulties inspire new solutions","explanation":"This proverb means that when there''s a need, people find ways to meet it.","points":1},{"id":5571,"question":"What does ''The pen is mightier than the sword'' mean?","options":["Writing is more powerful than violence","Pens are strong","Swords are weak","Write more"],"answer":"Writing is more powerful than violence","explanation":"This proverb means that communication has more influence than force.","points":1},{"id":5572,"question":"What does ''Look before you leap'' mean?","options":["Think carefully before acting","Jump far","Look around","Be brave"],"answer":"Think carefully before acting","explanation":"This proverb means to consider the consequences before taking action.","points":1},{"id":5573,"question":"What does ''Two wrongs don''t make a right'' mean?","options":["Retaliation doesn''t solve problems","Math is wrong","Be nice","Count twice"],"answer":"Retaliation doesn''t solve problems","explanation":"This proverb means that responding to a wrong with another wrong doesn''t make it okay.","points":1},{"id":5574,"question":"What does ''Absence makes the heart grow fonder'' mean?","options":["Being apart strengthens love","Hearts are strong","Go away","Miss someone"],"answer":"Being apart strengthens love","explanation":"This proverb means that time apart makes you appreciate someone more.","points":1},{"id":5575,"question":"What does ''The grass is always greener on the other side'' mean?","options":["Other people''s situations seem better than your own","Grass is green","Gardens are nice","Cross the fence"],"answer":"Other people''s situations seem better than your own","explanation":"This proverb means people tend to think others have it better than they do.","points":1},{"id":5576,"question":"What does ''Don''t judge a book by its cover'' mean?","options":["Don''t judge based on appearance","Books have covers","Read carefully","Covers are pretty"],"answer":"Don''t judge based on appearance","explanation":"This proverb means that outward appearances can be misleading.","points":1},{"id":5577,"question":"What does ''A watched pot never boils'' mean?","options":["Time seems slow when you''re waiting","Pots don''t boil","Watch carefully","Cook faster"],"answer":"Time seems slow when you''re waiting","explanation":"This proverb means that time seems to pass slowly when you''re anxiously waiting.","points":1},{"id":5578,"question":"What does ''Still waters run deep'' mean?","options":["Quiet people often have deep thoughts","Water is deep","Be still","Quiet is good"],"answer":"Quiet people often have deep thoughts","explanation":"This proverb means that calm-looking people often have complex inner lives.","points":1},{"id":5579,"question":"The ______ you practice, the ______ you will become.","options":["more, skilled","more, skill","skill, more","skilled, more"],"answer":"more, skilled","explanation":"Double comparative: the more you practice, the more skilled you will become.","points":1},{"id":5580,"question":"He ______ work hard if he wants to succeed.","options":["will have to","has to","must to","needs"],"answer":"will have to","explanation":"Future obligation: will have to.","points":1},{"id":5581,"question":"She ______ read the book yet.","options":["hasn''t","didn''t","wasn''t","doesn''t"],"answer":"hasn''t","explanation":"Present perfect negative with yet: hasn''t.","points":1},{"id":5582,"question":"The meeting was put ______ because of the storm.","options":["off","on","up","out"],"answer":"off","explanation":"Phrasal verb put off means to postpone.","points":1},{"id":5583,"question":"She looked ______ the window and saw a rainbow.","options":["out of","out from","outside of","out through"],"answer":"out of","explanation":"Look out of is the standard preposition phrase for windows.","points":1},{"id":5584,"question":"He always ______ his homework before dinner.","options":["does","makes","did","has"],"answer":"does","explanation":"Do homework is the correct collocation.","points":1}]'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (unit_id, slug) DO UPDATE SET type = EXCLUDED.type, instructions = EXCLUDED.instructions, questions = EXCLUDED.questions;

